@startuml
!define RECTANGLE class

RECTANGLE "Browser" as Browser {
  [Admin Application]
}

RECTANGLE "Server" as Server {
  [MyEMS REST API Service]
  [Database]
}

RECTANGLE "Deployment" as Deployment {
  [Nginx (Optional)]
  [Docker Environment]
}

[Browser] --> [Server] : HTTP/HTTPS\n/api/ requests
[Admin Application] --> [MyEMS REST API Service] : /api/ path resolution
[MyEMS REST API Service] --> [Database] : Persistent storage access

package "Admin Application Modules" {
  [User Settings Module]
  [Contact Settings Module]
  [Tariff Settings Module]
  [Category Settings Module]
}

[Admin Application] ..> [User Settings Module] : Lazy-loaded
[Admin Application] ..> [Contact Settings Module] : Lazy-loaded
[Admin Application] ..> [Tariff Settings Module] : Lazy-loaded (if configured)
[Admin Application] ..> [Category Settings Module] : Lazy-loaded (if configured)

note right of Server
  - Python runtime with dependencies
  - Supports Linux & Windows dev modes
  - Docker-based deployment supported
end note

note right of Deployment
  Optional reverse proxy like Nginx
  can route /api/ traffic to API service
end note

note top of Admin Application
  Routes:
  - /user (User Settings)
  - /contact (Contact Settings)
  - Others (Tariff, Category if enabled)
end note

note bottom of MyEMS REST API Service
  Provides RESTful endpoints for:
  - MyEMS components
  - Third-party applications
end note

@enduml
